From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: sleep instead of spinning while the firmware TX buffers are full

When the chip reports no free TX buffers, the flow-control loops polled it
30 times with udelay(200) before sleeping: up to 6 ms of busy waiting per
wait. During WebRTC video over Wi-Fi this was about 4 % of the C906 (udelay
in aicwf_bustx_thread). Both loops run in process context: the TX thread,
after down_interruptible(), and they issue SDIO reads, which may sleep. The
first 30 polls now use usleep_range(200, 300).

diff --git a/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c b/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
index ddcd1f5..3dc081c 100644
--- a/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
@@ -340,7 +340,7 @@ int aicwf_sdio_flow_ctrl_msg(struct aic_sdio_dev *sdiodev)
             }
             count++;
             if (count < 30)
-                udelay(200);
+                usleep_range(200, 300);
             else if(count < 40)
                 msleep(2);
             else
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@ int aicwf_sdio_flow_ctrl(struct aic_sdio_dev *sdiodev)
             }
             count++;
             if (count < 30)
-                udelay(200);
+                usleep_range(200, 300);
             else if(count < 40)
                 msleep(2);
             else
